# scry's memory-lifetime rule pack (CWE-416)
#
# A `kind memory` rule names the analysis with `check`; the analysis itself supplies
# the evidence path (allocation -> free -> use). Keep this pack separate from
# default.scry so enabling a lifetime claim is an explicit opt-in:
#
#   scry taint FILE.c --rules lib/Scry/rules/uaf.scry

rule scry/memory/use-after-free
  kind memory
  severity error
  message Memory is used after it was freed
  check use-after-free
end
